{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1038/nri3818\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"25720354","source":"MED","pmid":"25720354","pmcid":"PMC6314495","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC6314495"]},"doi":"10.1038/nri3818","title":"The ins and outs of MHC class II-mediated antigen processing and presentation.","authorString":"Roche PA, Furuta K.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Roche PA","lastName":"Roche","firstName":"Paul A","initials":"PA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8949-9172"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Experimental Immunology Branch, National Cancer Institute, National Institutes of Health, Bethesda, Maryland 20892-9760, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Furuta K","lastName":"Furuta","firstName":"Kazuyuki","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunobiology, Okayama University Graduate School of Medicine, Dentistry, and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Okayama University, Okayama 7008530, Japan."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8949-9172"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","recommended_reviews","related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"15","journalIssueId":2267697,"dateOfPublication":"2015 Apr","monthOfPublication":4,"yearOfPublication":2015,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Nat Rev Immunol","title":"Nature reviews. Immunology","essn":"1474-1741","issn":"1474-1733","isoabbreviation":"Nat Rev Immunol","nlmid":"101124169"},"printPublicationDate":"2015-04-01"},"pubYear":"2015","pageInfo":"203-216","abstractText":"Antigenic peptide-loaded MHC class II molecules (peptide-MHC class II) are constitutively expressed on the surface of professional antigen-presenting cells (APCs), including dendritic cells, B cells, macrophages and thymic epithelial cells, and are presented to antigen-specific CD4(+) T cells. The mechanisms of antigen uptake, the nature of the antigen processing compartments and the lifetime of cell surface peptide-MHC class II complexes can vary depending on the type of APC. It is likely that these differences are important for the function of each distinct APC subset in the generation of effective adaptive immune responses. In this Review, we describe our current knowledge of the mechanisms of uptake and processing of antigens, the intracellular formation of peptide-MHC class II complexes, the intracellular trafficking of peptide-MHC class II complexes to the APC plasma membrane and their ultimate degradation.","affiliation":"Experimental Immunology Branch, National Cancer Institute, National Institutes of Health, Bethesda, Maryland 20892-9760, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Intramural NIH HHS","acronym":"ImNIH","grantId":"Z01 BC009404","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Intramural NIH HHS","acronym":"ImNIH","grantId":"Z01 BC011033","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Antigen-Presenting Cells","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Membrane","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Peptides","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Antigens","meshQualifierList":{"mesh